n\\[\nDE = \\sqrt{51}\n\\]\n\nSo, the length of \\(DE\\) is \\(\\sqrt{51}\\). Let's confirm this using Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given values\nsin_D = 0.7\nEF = 7\n\n# Calculate the hypotenuse DF\nDF = EF / sin_D\n\n# Use the Pythagorean theorem to find DE\nDE = math.sqrt(DF**2 - EF**2)\nprint(DE)\n```\n```output\n7.14142842854285\n```\nThe calculated value of \\(DE\\) is approximately \\(7.14142842854285\\), which is \\(\\sqrt{51}\\). Therefore, the length of \\(DE\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\sqrt{51}}\n\\]", "To find the length of \\(DE\\) in the right triangle \\(DEF\\) where \\(\\sin D = 0.7\\) and \\(EF = 7\\), we can use the definition of sine in a right triangle. The sine of an angle in a right triangle is the ratio of the length of the opposite side to the hypotenuse. In this case, \\(\\sin D = \\frac{EF}{DE}\\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\sin D = 0.7 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad EF = 7\n\\]\n\nWe can set up the equation:\n\\[\n0.7 = \\frac{7}{DE}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(DE\\):\n\\[\nDE = \\frac{7}{0.7} = 10\n\\]\n\nSo, the length of \\(DE\\) is \\(10\\). Let's confirm this with Python code for accuracy.\n```python\n# Given values\nsin_D = 0.7\nEF = 7\n\n# Calculate DE\nDE = EF / sin_D\nprint(DE)\n```\n```output\n10.0\n```\nThe length of \\(DE\\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).", "To find the length of \\(DE\\), we can use the definition of the sine function in a right triangle. In the right triangle \\(DEF\\), the sine of angle \\(D\\) is given by the ratio of the length of the opposite side to the hypotenuse. Here, the opposite side to angle \\(D\\) is \\(EF\\) and the hypotenuse is \\(DF\\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\sin D = 0.7\n\\]\n\\[\nEF = 7\n\\]\nWe need to find \\(DE\\).\n\nSince \\(\\sin D = \\frac{EF}{DF}\\), we have:\n\\[\n0.7 = \\frac{7}{DF}\n\\]\nFrom this, we can solve for \\(DF\\):\n\\[\nDF = \\frac{7}{0.7} = 10\n\\]\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean theorem to find \\(DE\\):\n\\[\nDF^2 = DE^2 + EF^2\n\\]\n\\[\n10^2 = DE^2 + 7^2\n\\]\n\\[\n100 = DE^2 + 49\n\\]\n\\[\nDE^2 = 100 - 49 = 51\n\\]\n\\[\nDE = \\sqrt{51}\n\\]\n\nSo, the length of \\(DE\\) is \\(\\sqrt{51}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given values\nsin_D = 0.7\nEF = 7\n\n# Calculate DF\nDF = EF / sin_D\n\n# Calculate DE using the Pythagorean theorem\nDE = math.sqrt(DF**2 - EF**2)\nprint(DE)\n```\n```output\n7.14142842854285\n```\nThe calculated length of \\(DE\\) is approximately \\(7.14142842854285\\), which matches \\(\\sqrt{51}\\). Therefore, the exact length of \\(DE\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\sqrt{51}}\n\\]", '^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^\n^