ct to base 8\nproduct_base8 = to_base8(product_base10)\nprint(product_base8)\n```\n```output\n52\n```\nThe product of \\(6_8 \\cdot 7_8\\) in base 8 is \\(\\boxed{52_8}\\).', 'To find the product of \\(6_8 \\cdot 7_8\\) and express the answer in base 8, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the base 8 numbers to base 10.\n2. Perform the multiplication in base 10.\n3. Convert the result back to base 8.\n\nLet\'s go through these steps one by one.\n\n1. Convert \\(6_8\\) and \\(7_8\\) to base 10.\n   - \\(6_8 = 6 \\cdot 8^0 = 6_{10}\\)\n   - \\(7_8 = 7 \\cdot 8^0 = 7_{10}\\)\n\n2. Perform the multiplication in base 10.\n   - \\(6_{10} \\cdot 7_{10} = 42_{10}\\)\n\n3. Convert \\(42_{10}\\) back to base 8.\n   - To convert a number from base 10 to base 8, we repeatedly divide the number by 8 and keep track of the remainders.\n   - \\(42 \\div 8 = 5\\) remainder \\(2\\)\n   - \\(5 \\div 8 = 0\\) remainder \\(5\\)\n   - Reading the remainders in reverse order, we get \\(52_8\\).\n\nSo, the product of \\(6_8 \\cdot 7_8\\) in base 8 is \\(52_8\\).\n\nLet\'s verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Function to convert a base 10 number to base 8\ndef to_base_8(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return "0"\n    digits = []\n    while n:\n        digits.append(int(n % 8))\n        n //= 8\n    return \'\'.join(str(x) for x in digits[::-1])\n\n# Base 10 values of 6_8 and 7_8\nnum1 = 6\nnum2 = 7\n\n# Perform multiplication in base 10\nproduct_base_10 = num1 * num2\n\n# Convert the product to base 8\nproduct_base_8 = to_base_8(product_base_10)\nprint(product_base_8)\n```\n```output\n52\n```\nThe product of \\(6_8 \\cdot 7_8\\) in base 8 is \\(\\boxed{52_8}\\).', 'To solve the problem of multiplying \\(6_8 \\cdot 7_8\\) and expressing the answer in base 8, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Convert the base 8 numbers to base 10.\n2. Perform the multiplication in base 10.\n3. Convert the result back to base 8.\n\nLet\'s break it down:\n\n1. Convert \\(6_8\\) and \\(