\n2. The perimeter of the octagon is the same as that of the hexagon, so the perimeter \\(P_{\\text{octagon}}\\) is also 96 cm. Since an octagon has 8 sides, the side length \\(s\\) of the octagon can be found by dividing the perimeter by 8:\n\\[ s = \\frac{P_{\\text{octagon}}}{8} = \\frac{96}{8} = 12 \\text{ cm} \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given side length of the hexagon\nside_length_hexagon = 16\n\n# Number of sides of the hexagon\nnum_sides_hexagon = 6\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the hexagon\nperimeter_hexagon = side_length_hexagon * num_sides_hexagon\n\n# Number of sides of the octagon\nnum_sides_octagon = 8\n\n# Calculate the side length of the octagon\nside_length_octagon = perimeter_hexagon / num_sides_octagon\nprint(side_length_octagon)\n```\n```output\n12.0\n```\nThe side length of the octagon is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) cm.", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the side length of a regular octagon that has the same perimeter as a regular hexagon with a side length of 16 cm.\n\n1. First, we calculate the perimeter of the hexagon.\n2. Then, we use the perimeter of the hexagon to find the side length of the octagon.\n\nA regular hexagon has 6 sides. If each side of the hexagon is 16 cm, then the perimeter of the hexagon is \\(6 \\times 16 = 96\\) cm.\n\nA regular octagon has 8 sides. If the perimeter of the octagon is 96 cm, then the side length of the octagon is \\(\\frac{96}{8} = 12\\) cm.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Given side length of the hexagon\nside_length_hexagon = 16\n\n# Number of sides of the hexagon\nnum_sides_hexagon = 6\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of the hexagon\nperimeter_hexagon = side_length_hexagon * num_sides_hexagon\n\n# Number of sides of the octagon\nnum_sides_octagon = 8\n\n# Calculate the side length of the octagon\nside_length_octagon = perimeter_hexagon / num_sides_octagon\nprint(side_length_octagon)\n```\n```output\n12.0\n```\nThe side length of the octagon is \\(\\box