uation \\((x-1) \\cdot f(x) = 3x^4 + x^3 - 25x^2 + 38x - 17\\).\n\nThe degree of the polynomial on the right-hand side is 4. When we multiply \\( f(x) \\) by \\((x-1)\\), the degree of the resulting polynomial will be one more than the degree of \\( f(x) \\). Therefore, if the degree of \\( f(x) \\) is \\( n \\), then the degree of \\((x-1) \\cdot f(x)\\) will be \\( n+1 \\).\n\nSince the degree of \\((x-1) \\cdot f(x)\\) is 4, the degree of \\( f(x) \\) must be \\( 4 - 1 = 3 \\).\n\nThus, the degree of \\( f(x) \\) is 3.\n\nLet's confirm this by performing polynomial division in Python to find \\( f(x) \\).\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable and the polynomials\nx = sp.symbols('x')\nnumerator = 3*x**4 + x**3 - 25*x**2 + 38*x - 17\ndenominator = x - 1\n\n# Perform polynomial division\nquotient, remainder = sp.div(numerator, denominator)\n\nprint((quotient, remainder))\n```\n```output\n(3*x**3 + 4*x**2 - 21*x + 17, 0)\n```\nThe polynomial division of \\(3x^4 + x^3 - 25x^2 + 38x - 17\\) by \\(x - 1\\) gives a quotient of \\(3x^3 + 4x^2 - 21x + 17\\) and a remainder of 0. This confirms that \\(f(x) = 3x^3 + 4x^2 - 21x + 17\\).\n\nSince the degree of \\(3x^3 + 4x^2 - 21x + 17\\) is 3, the degree of \\(f(x)\\) is indeed 3.\n\nThus, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).", "To determine the degree of the polynomial \\( f(x) \\), we need to analyze the given equation:\n\n\\[\n(x-1) \\cdot f(x) = 3x^4 + x^3 - 25x^2 + 38x - 17.\n\\]\n\nFirst, let's denote the degree of \\( f(x) \\) as \\( \\deg(f) \\). The degree of the left-hand side of the equation, \\((x-1) \\cdot f(x)\\), is the sum of the degrees of \\((x-1)\\) and \\( f(x) \\). Since the degree of \\((x-1)\\) is 1, the degree of the left-hand side is \\( 1 + \\deg(f) \\).\n\nThe degree of the right-hand side of the equation, \\(3x^4 + x^3 - 25x^2 + 38x - 17\\), is 4 (since the highest power of \\(x\\) is 4).\n\nSince the degrees of both sides of the equation must be equal, we have:\n\n\\[\n1 + \\deg