al number of outfits is:\n\\[ \\text{Total outfits} = \\text{Number of shirts} \\times \\text{Number of pairs of pants} \\times \\text{Number of hats} \\]\n\nGiven:\n- Number of shirts = 5\n- Number of pairs of pants = 6\n- Number of hats = 8\n\nThe total number of outfits can be calculated as:\n\\[ \\text{Total outfits} = 5 \\times 6 \\times 8 \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Number of shirts, pairs of pants, and hats\nnum_shirts = 5\nnum_pants = 6\nnum_hats = 8\n\n# Total number of outfits\ntotal_outfits = num_shirts * num_pants * num_hats\nprint(total_outfits)\n```\n```output\n240\n```\nThe total number of outfits that can be made consisting of one shirt, one pair of pants, and one hat is \\(\\boxed{240}\\).", "To determine the total number of outfits that can be made from 5 shirts, 6 pairs of pants, and 8 hats, we need to calculate the product of the number of choices for each item. This is because for each shirt, there are 6 choices of pants and 8 choices of hats.\n\nThe total number of outfits is given by:\n\\[ \\text{Total outfits} = \\text{Number of shirts} \\times \\text{Number of pants} \\times \\text{Number of hats} \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python code.\n```python\n# Number of shirts, pants, and hats\nnum_shirts = 5\nnum_pants = 6\nnum_hats = 8\n\n# Total number of outfits\ntotal_outfits = num_shirts * num_pants * num_hats\nprint(total_outfits)\n```\n```output\n240\n```\nThe total number of outfits that can be made consisting of one shirt, one pair of pants, and one hat is \\(\\boxed{240}\\).", "To determine the number of different outfits that can be made from 5 shirts, 6 pairs of pants, and 8 hats, we can use the fundamental counting principle. The fundamental counting principle states that if there are \\(m\\) ways to do one thing, and \\(n\\) ways to do another, then there are \\(m \\times n\\) ways to do both.\n\nIn this case, we have:\n- 5 choices for shirts\n- 6 choices for pants\n- 8 choices for hats\n\nSo, the total number of different outfits can be calculated by multiplying these choices together:\n\n\\[ \\text{Total outfits} = 5 \\times 6 \\times 8 \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Number of shirts, pants, and hats\nshirts = 5\npants = 6\nhats = 8\n\n# Total number of outfits\ntotal_outfits = shirts * pants * hats\nprint(total_outfits)\n```\n```output\n240\n```\nThe total number of different outfits that can be made consisting of one shirt, one pair of pants, and one hat is \\(\\boxed{240}\\).", "To determine the total number of outfits you can make consisting of one shirt, one pair of pants, and one hat, we can use the fundamental principle of counting. This principle states that if there are \\(m\\) ways to do one thing, and \\(n\\) ways to do another, then there are \\(m \\times n\\) ways to do both.\n\nIn this problem:\n- There are 5 shirts.\n- There are 6 pairs of pants.\n- There are 8 hats.\n\nSo, the total number of outfits can be calculated as:\n\\[ \\text{Total outfits} = 5 \\times 6 \\times 8 \\]\n\nLet's compute this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Number of shirts\nnum_shirts = 5\n\n# Number of pairs of pants\nnum_pants = 6\n\n# Number of hats\nnum_hats = 8\n\n# Total number of outfits\ntotal_outfits = num_shirts * num_pants * num_hats\nprint(total_outfits)\n```\n```output\n240\n```\nThe total number of outfits you can make consisting of one shirt, one pair of pants, and one hat is \\(\\boxed{240}\\).", "To determine the total number of outfits that can be made from 5 shirts, 6 pairs of pants, and 8 hats, we need to calculate the product of the number of choices for each item of clothing. This is because each shirt can be paired with each pair of pants, and each of those combinations can be paired with each hat.\n\nThe formula for the total number of outfits is:\n\\[ \\text{Total outfits} = (\\text{Number of shirts}) \\times (\\text{Number of pants}) \\times (\\text{Number of hats}) \\]\