 circle, opposite angles sum to \\(180^\\circ\\). Therefore, the remaining three angles are \\(180^\\circ - 105^\\circ = 75^\\circ\\), \\(180^\\circ - 110^\\circ = 70^\\circ\\), and \\(180^\\circ - \\alpha\\). The sum of these three angles should be \\(505^\\circ - 180^\\circ = 325^\\circ\\). So we have:\n\\[75^\\circ + 70^\\circ + (180^\\circ - \\alpha) = 325^\\circ\\]\n\\[325^\\circ - \\alpha = 325^\\circ\\]\n\\[\\alpha = 180^\\circ - 75^\\circ - 70^\\circ\\]\n\\[\\alpha = 35^\\circ\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with a simpler Python code.\n```python\n# Given angles in the hexagon\r\nangle1 = 105\r\nangle2 = 110\r\n\r\n# Since the hexagon is inscribed in a circle, opposite angles sum to 180 degrees\r\n# So the remaining three angles are 180 - angle1, 180 - angle2, and 180 - alpha\r\n# The sum of these three angles should be 505 degrees minus 180 degrees (since opposite angles sum to 180 degrees)\r\n# Therefore, (180 - angle1) + (180 - angle2) + (180 - alpha) = 505 - 180\r\n# Simplifying, we get 540 - (angle1 + angle2) - alpha = 325\r\n# So, alpha = 540 - (angle1 + angle2) - 325\r\n\r\nalpha = 180 - (180 - angle1) - (180 - angle2)\r\nprint(alpha)\n```\n```output\n35\n```\nThe measure of \\(\\alpha\\) is indeed \\(35^\\circ\\). Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{35}\n\\]", "To solve the problem, we need to use the properties of a cyclic hexagon and the fact that the sum of the interior angles of a hexagon is \\(720^\\circ\\). For a cyclic hexagon, the opposite angles sum to \\(180^\\circ\\). Let's denote the angles of the hexagon as follows:\n\n- \\(\\angle F = 105^\\circ\\)\n- \\(\\angle B = 110^\\circ\\)\n- \\(\\angle A + \\angle D = 180^\\circ\\) (since they are opposite angles in a cyclic hexagon)\n- \\(\\angle C + \\angle E = 180^\\circ\\) (since they are opposite angles in a cyclic hexagon)\n\nThe sum of the interior angles of a hexagon is \\(720^\\circ\\). So we have:\n\n\\[\n\\angle A + \\angle B + \\angle C + \\angle D + \\angle E + \\angle F = 720^