 of \\( |m - n| \\) given the equation \\( 3m + 4n = 100 \\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Express \\( m \\) in terms of \\( n \\) (or vice versa) using the equation \\( 3m + 4n = 100 \\).\n2. Iterate over possible integer values of \\( n \\) to find corresponding integer values of \\( m \\).\n3. Calculate \\( |m - n| \\) for each pair \\((m, n)\\) and find the minimum value.\n\nLet's start by expressing \\( m \\) in terms of \\( n \\):\n\\[ m = \\frac{100 - 4n}{3} \\]\nFor \\( m \\) to be an integer, \\( 100 - 4n \\) must be divisible by 3. This means \\( 100 - 4n \\equiv 0 \\pmod{3} \\), or equivalently, \\( 4n \\equiv 100 \\pmod{3} \\). Since \\( 100 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3} \\) and \\( 4 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3} \\), we have \\( n \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3} \\). So \\( n \\) can be written as \\( n = 3k + 1 \\) for some integer \\( k \\).\n\nNow, we can substitute \\( n = 3k + 1 \\) into the equation for \\( m \\):\n\\[ m = \\frac{100 - 4(3k + 1)}{3} = \\frac{100 - 12k - 4}{3} = \\frac{96 - 12k}{3} = 32 - 4k \\]\nSo, the pairs \\((m, n)\\) are of the form \\((32 - 4k, 3k + 1)\\).\n\nNext, we need to find the value of \\( k \\) that minimizes \\( |m - n| \\):\n\\[ |m - n| = |(32 - 4k) - (3k + 1)| = |31 - 7k| \\]\nWe need to find the integer \\( k \\) that minimizes \\( |31 - 7k| \\). The closest multiple of 7 to 31 is 28 (since \\( 7 \\times 4 = 28 \\)). So, \\( k = 4 \\) is a good candidate. Let's check the values around \\( k = 4 \\) to ensure we have the minimum.\n\nFor \\( k = 4 \\):\n\\[ |31 - 7 \\cdot 4| = |31 - 28| = 3 \\]\n\nFor \\( k = 3 \\):\n\\[ |31 - 7 \\cdot 3| = |31 - 21| = 10 \\]\n\nFor \\( k = 5 \\):\n\\[ |31 - 7 \\cdot 5| = |31 - 35| = 4 \\]\n\nSo, the smallest possible value of \\( |m - n| \\) is 3, which occurs when \\( k = 4 \\). Let's verify this by calculating the corresponding \\( m \\) and \\( n \\):\n\\[ n = 3 \\cdot 4 + 1 = 13 \\]\n\\[ m = 32 - 4 \\cdot 4 = 16 \\]\n\\[ |m - n| = |16 - 13| = 3 \\]\n\nThus, the smallest possible value of \\( |m - n| \\