th 150 m, so the distance from \\(H\\) to \\(C\\) is 150 m. Since \\(H\\) is directly above \\(O\\) at \\((0, h)\\), the distance \\(HC\\) is \\(\\sqrt{0^2 + h^2 + c^2} = 150\\). So, \\(h^2 + c^2 = 150^2\\).\n   - Rope \\(HD\\) has length 130 m, so the distance from \\(H\\) to \\(D\\) is 130 m. The distance \\(HD\\) is \\(\\sqrt{0^2 + h^2 + d^2} = 130\\). So, \\(h^2 + d^2 = 130^2\\).\n\n3. **Solve for \\(h\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\):**\n   - From \\(d + c = 140\\), we get \\(d = 140 - c\\).\n   - Substitute \\(d = 140 - c\\) into \\(h^2 + d^2 = 130^2\\):\n     \\[\n     h^2 + (140 - c)^2 = 130^2.\n     \\]\n   - We also have \\(h^2 + c^2 = 150^2\\). So, we can solve these equations to find \\(h\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\).\n\n4. **Find the Length of Rope \\(HP\\):**\n   - The new rope \\(HP\\) will be along the line segment \\(CD\\). Let \\(P\\) be a point on \\(CD\\) such that \\(P = (x, 0)\\). The distance \\(HP\\) is \\(\\sqrt{0^2 + h^2 + x^2}\\). We need to find the length of \\(HP\\) and compare it to the sum of \\(HC\\) and \\(HD\\).\n\nLet's solve this using Python and sympy.\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define variables\nh, c, d = sp.symbols('h c d')\n\n# Equations based on the given conditions\neq1 = sp.Eq(h**2 + c**2, 150**2)\neq2 = sp.Eq(h**2 + d**2, 130**2)\neq3 = sp.Eq(d + c, 140)\n\n# Solve the system of equations\nsolution = sp.solve((eq1, eq2, eq3), (h, c, d))\nh_val, c_val, d_val = solution[0]\n\n# Calculate the length of the new rope HP\n# P is on the line segment CD, so P = (x, 0) where x is between -d and c\n# The length of HP is sqrt(h^2 + x^2)\n# We need to find the maximum length of HP, which is the minimum of HC and HD\n# Since P is on the line segment CD, the length of HP will be minimized when P is at the point that minimizes the distance to H\n# The length of HP will be the perpendicular distance from H to the line CD, which is the same as the length of the altitude from H to CD\n\n# The length of the altitude from H to CD is the same 