Using the formula for the magnitude of the cross product, we have:\n\\[\n7 = 2 \\cdot 7 \\cdot \\sin(\\theta)\n\\]\nSimplifying, we get:\n\\[\n7 = 14 \\sin(\\theta) \\implies \\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\nThe angle \\(\\theta\\) for which \\(\\sin(\\theta) = \\frac{1}{2}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\theta = \\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\n\\]\nThe smallest possible angle in degrees is:\n\\[\n\\theta = 30^\\circ\n\\]\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given magnitudes and cross product\nnorm_a = 2\nnorm_b = 7\ncross_product = [3, 2, 6]\n\n# Calculate the magnitude of the cross product\nmagnitude_cross_product = math.sqrt(sum([x**2 for x in cross_product]))\n\n# Calculate sin(theta)\nsin_theta = magnitude_cross_product / (norm_a * norm_b)\n\n# Calculate theta in radians and then convert to degrees\ntheta_radians = math.asin(sin_theta)\ntheta_degrees = math.degrees(theta_radians)\n\nprint(theta_degrees)\n```\n```output\n30.000000000000004\n```\nThe smallest possible angle between the vectors \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\) is \\(\\boxed{30}\\) degrees.", "To find the smallest possible angle between vectors \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), we can use the properties of the cross product. Recall that the magnitude of the cross product of two vectors \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\| = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\sin(\\theta)\n\\]\n\nwhere \\(\\theta\\) is the angle between the vectors \\(\\mathbf{a}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b}\\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| = 2, \\quad \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| = 7, \\quad \\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we need to find the magnitude of the cross product vector \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\| = \\sqrt{3^2 + 2^2 + 6^2}\n\\]\n\nNext, we can use the formula for the magnitude of the cross product to find \\(\\sin(