 4006 - 1 = 4005 \\]\n\nLet's verify this using Python code.\n```python\n# Define the term number\nn = 2003\n\n# Calculate the 2003rd term of the sequence of odd numbers\nterm = 2 * n - 1\nprint(term)\n```\n```output\n4005\n```\nThe 2003rd term of the sequence of odd numbers \\(1, 3, 5, 7, \\ldots\\) is \\(\\boxed{4005}\\).", "To find the 2003rd term of the sequence of odd numbers, we can use the formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence. The general formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[ a_n = a_1 + (n-1)d \\]\nwhere:\n- \\(a_n\\) is the \\(n\\)-th term,\n- \\(a_1\\) is the first term,\n- \\(d\\) is the common difference,\n- \\(n\\) is the term number.\n\nFor the sequence of odd numbers 1, 3, 5, 7, \\(\\dots\\):\n- The first term \\(a_1 = 1\\),\n- The common difference \\(d = 2\\),\n- The term number \\(n = 2003\\).\n\nPlugging these values into the formula, we get:\n\\[ a_{2003} = 1 + (2003-1) \\cdot 2 \\]\n\\[ a_{2003} = 1 + 2002 \\cdot 2 \\]\n\\[ a_{2003} = 1 + 4004 \\]\n\\[ a_{2003} = 4005 \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the first term and the common difference\na1 = 1\nd = 2\nn = 2003\n\n# Calculate the 2003rd term\na_n = a1 + (n - 1) * d\nprint(a_n)\n```\n```output\n4005\n```\nThe 2003rd term of the sequence of odd numbers is \\(\\boxed{4005}\\).", "The sequence of odd numbers can be expressed as \\(a_n = 2n - 1\\), where \\(n\\) is the position of the term in the sequence. To find the 2003rd term, we need to substitute \\(n = 2003\\) into the formula. Let's calculate it using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the formula for the nth term of the sequence of odd numbers\ndef nth_odd_number(n):\n    return 2 * n - 1\n\n# Calculate the 2003rd term\nterm_2003 = nth_odd_number(2003)\nprint(term_2003)\n```\n```output\n4005\n```\nThe 2003rd term of the sequence of odd numbers is \\(\\boxed{4005}\\).", "To find the 2003rd term of the sequence of odd numbers, we can use