s $9 \\times 2 = 18$ units. The "band" around the nonagon adds an additional 1 unit on each side, so the perimeter of the band is the same as the perimeter of the nonagon but with each side increased by 2 units (1 unit on each side). Therefore, the perimeter of the band is also $18$ units.\n\nThe total perimeter of the set $S$ is the sum of the perimeter of the nonagon and the perimeter of the band. However, since the band is a continuous region around the nonagon, the perimeter of the band is already included in the perimeter of the nonagon when we consider the outer boundary of the set $S$. Therefore, the perimeter of $S$ is simply the perimeter of the nonagon, which is $18$ units.\n\nLet\'s confirm this with a simple Python code to ensure the calculation is correct.\n```python\n# Side length of the nonagon\nside_length = 2\n\n# Number of sides of the nonagon\nnum_sides = 9\n\n# Perimeter of the nonagon\nperimeter_nonagon = side_length * num_sides\n\n# The perimeter of the set S is the same as the perimeter of the nonagon\nperimeter_S = perimeter_nonagon\n\nprint(perimeter_S)\n```\n```output\n18\n```\nThe perimeter of the set $S$ is \\(\\boxed{36}\\).', 'To solve the problem, we need to find the perimeter of the set \\( S \\) which includes all points inside a regular nonagon with side length 2 units and all points less than 1 unit away from a point on the perimeter of the nonagon. This means that the set \\( S \\) is essentially a region that includes the nonagon itself and a 1-unit wide "band" around the nonagon.\n\nThe perimeter of \\( S \\) will be the perimeter of the nonagon plus the perimeter of the 1-unit wide band around the nonagon. Since the nonagon has 9 sides, each of length 2 units, the perimeter of the nonagon is \\( 9 \\times 2 = 18 \\) units. The 1-unit wide band around the nonagon will add an additional perimeter of \\( 9 \\times 2 = 18 \\) units (since the band wraps around each side of the nonagon). Therefore, the total perimeter of \\( S \\) i