_3 + x_2 - x_1 = 523 - 420 + 375 - 211 = 267\\)\n6. \\(x_6 = x_5 - x_4 + x_3 - x_2 = 267 - 523 + 420 - 375 = -211\\)\n7. \\(x_7 = x_6 - x_5 + x_4 - x_3 = -211 - 267 + 523 - 420 = -375\\)\n8. \\(x_8 = x_7 - x_6 + x_5 - x_4 = -375 - (-211) + 267 - 523 = -420\\)\n9. \\(x_9 = x_8 - x_7 + x_6 - x_5 = -420 - (-375) + (-211) - 267 = -523\\)\n10. \\(x_{10} = x_9 - x_8 + x_7 - x_6 = -523 - (-420) + (-375) - (-211) = -267\\)\n11. \\(x_{11} = x_{10} - x_9 + x_8 - x_7 = -267 - (-523) + (-420) - (-375) = 211\\)\n12. \\(x_{12} = x_{11} - x_{10} + x_9 - x_8 = 211 - (-267) + (-523) - (-420) = 375\\)\n\nWe can see that the sequence repeats every 10 terms. Therefore, we can use the periodicity to find \\(x_{531}\\), \\(x_{753}\\), and \\(x_{975}\\).\n\n1. \\(x_{531} = x_{531 \\mod 10} = x_1 = 211\\)\n2. \\(x_{753} = x_{753 \\mod 10} = x_3 = 420\\)\n3. \\(x_{975} = x_{975 \\mod 10} = x_5 = 267\\)\n\nFinally, we sum these values:\n\\[x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975} = 211 + 420 + 267 = 898\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the initial values\nx = [211, 375, 420, 523]\n\n# Calculate the next terms until we have enough to confirm the periodicity\nfor n in range(4, 20):\n    x_n = x[n-1] - x[n-2] + x[n-3] - x[n-4]\n    x.append(x_n)\n\n# Check the periodicity\nperiod = 10  # Based on the observed pattern\n\n# Calculate the values of x_531, x_753, and x_975\nx_531 = x[531 % period - 1]\nx_753 = x[753 % period - 1]\nx_975 = x[975 % period - 1]\n\n# Sum the values\nresult = x_531 + x_753 + x_975\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n898\n```\nThe value of \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\) is \\(\\boxed{898}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to determine the value of \\(x_{531}\\), \\(x_{753}\\), and \\(x_{975}\\) using the given recurrence relation, and then sum these values. The recurrence relation is defined as:\n\\[ x_n = x_{n-1} - x_{n-2} + x_{n-3} - x_{n-4} \\text{ for } n \\geq 5. \\]\n\nLet's start by calculating the first few terms of the sequence to identify any patterns. We are given the initial values:\n\\[ x_1 = 211, \\]\n\\[ x_2 = 375, \\]\n\\[ x_3 = 420, \\]\n\\[ x_4 = 523. \\]\n\nUsing the recurrence relation, we can calculate the next terms:\n\\[ x_5 = x_4 - x_3 + x_2 - x_1 = 523 - 420 + 375 - 211 = 267, \\]\n\\[ x_6 = x_5 - x_4 + x_3 - x_2 = 267 - 523 + 420 - 375 = -211, \\]\n\\[ x_7 = x_6 - x_5 + x_4 - x_3 = -211 - 267 + 523 - 420 = -375, \\]\n\\[ x_8 = x_7 - x_6 + x_5 - x_4 = -375 - (-211) + 267 - 523 = -420, \\]\n\\[ x_9 = x_8 - x_7 + x_6 - x_5 = -420 - (-375) + (-211) - 267 = -523, \\]\n\\[ x_{10} = x_9 - x_8 + x_7 - x_6 = -523 - (-420) + (-375) - (-211) = -267, \\]\n\\[ x_{11} = x_{10} - x_9 + x_8 - x_7 = -267 - (-523) + (-420) - (-375) = 211, \\]\n\\[ x_{12} = x_{11} - x_{10} + x_9 - x_8 = 211 - (-267) + (-523) - (-420) = 375. \\]\n\nWe can see that \\(x_{11} = x_1\\) and \\(x_{12} = x_2\\), which suggests that the sequence is periodic with a period of 10. Therefore, we can write:\n\\[ x_{n} = x_{n \\mod 10} \\text{ for } n \\geq 1. \\]\n\nUsing this periodicity, we can find:\n\\[ x_{531} = x_{531 \\mod 10} = x_1 = 211, \\]\n\\[ x_{753} = x_{753 \\mod 10} = x_3 = 420, \\]\n\\[ x_{975} = x_{975 \\mod 10} = x_5 = 267. \\]\n\nThus, the sum \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\) is:\n\\[ 211 + 420 + 267 = 898. \\]\n\nLet's confirm this by implementing the solution in Python.\n```python\n# Initial values\nx = [211, 375, 420, 523]\n\n# Calculate the first 10 terms to confirm the periodicity\nfor n in range(4, 10):\n    x.append(x[n-1] - x[n-2] + x[n-3] - x[n-4])\n\n# Periodicity is 10, so we can find x_531, x_753, and x_975 using the periodicity\nx_531 = x[531 % 10 - 1]\nx_753 = x[753 % 10 - 1]\nx_975 = x[975 % 10 - 1]\n\n# Calculate the sum\nresult = x_531 + x_753 + x_975\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n898\n```\nThe value of \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\) is \\(\\boxed{898}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to compute the sequence values up to the required indices. Let's break it down step-b