tterns:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nx_5 &= x_4 - x_3 + x_2 - x_1 = 523 - 420 + 375 - 211 = 267, \\\\\nx_6 &= x_5 - x_4 + x_3 - x_2 = 267 - 523 + 420 - 375 = -211, \\\\\nx_7 &= x_6 - x_5 + x_4 - x_3 = -211 - 267 + 523 - 420 = -375, \\\\\nx_8 &= x_7 - x_6 + x_5 - x_4 = -375 - (-211) + 267 - 523 = -420, \\\\\nx_9 &= x_8 - x_7 + x_6 - x_5 = -420 - (-375) + (-211) - 267 = -523, \\\\\nx_{10} &= x_9 - x_8 + x_7 - x_6 = -523 - (-420) + (-375) - (-211) = -267, \\\\\nx_{11} &= x_{10} - x_9 + x_8 - x_7 = -267 - (-523) + (-420) - (-375) = 211, \\\\\nx_{12} &= x_{11} - x_{10} + x_9 - x_8 = 211 - (-267) + (-523) - (-420) = 375.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nWe can see that \\(x_{11} = x_1\\) and \\(x_{12} = x_2\\). This suggests that the sequence repeats every 10 terms. Therefore, we can conclude that \\(x_{n} = x_{n \\mod 10}\\) for \\(n \\geq 1\\).\n\nNow, we can find the values of \\(x_{531}\\), \\(x_{753}\\), and \\(x_{975}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nx_{531} &= x_{531 \\mod 10} = x_1 = 211, \\\\\nx_{753} &= x_{753 \\mod 10} = x_3 = 420, \\\\\nx_{975} &= x_{975 \\mod 10} = x_5 = 267.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nSo, the value of \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\) is \\(211 + 420 + 267 = 898\\).\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{898}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to first compute the values of the sequence up to the required indices. We are given the initial values \\(x_1 = 211\\), \\(x_2 = 375\\), \\(x_3 = 420\\), and \\(x_4 = 523\\). For \\(n \\geq 5\\), the sequence is defined as \\(x_n = x_{n-1} - x_{n-2} + x_{n-3} - x_{n-4}\\).\n\nLet's write a Python function to compute the values of the sequence and then find \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\).\n\n```python\ndef compute_sequence(n):\n    # Initial values\n    x = [0] * (n + 1)\n    x[1] = 211\n    x[2] = 375\n    x[3] = 420\n    x[4] = 523\n    \n    # Compute the sequence values\n    for i in range(5, n + 1):\n        x[i] = x[i - 1] - x[i - 2] + x[i - 3] - x[i - 4]\n    \n    return x\n\n# Compute the sequence up to x_975\nseq