 - x_4 = -375 - (-211) + 267 - 523 = -420, \\]\n\\[ x_9 = x_8 - x_7 + x_6 - x_5 = -420 - (-375) + (-211) - 267 = -523, \\]\n\\[ x_{10} = x_9 - x_8 + x_7 - x_6 = -523 - (-420) + (-375) - (-211) = -267, \\]\n\\[ x_{11} = x_{10} - x_9 + x_8 - x_7 = -267 - (-523) + (-420) - (-375) = 211, \\]\n\\[ x_{12} = x_{11} - x_{10} + x_9 - x_8 = 211 - (-267) + (-523) - (-420) = 375. \\]\n\nWe observe that \\(x_{11} = x_1\\) and \\(x_{12} = x_2\\). This suggests that the sequence is periodic with a period of 10. Therefore, we can write:\n\n\\[ x_{n} = x_{n \\mod 10} \\text{ for } n \\geq 1. \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the values of \\(x_{531}\\), \\(x_{753}\\), and \\(x_{975}\\):\n\n\\[ x_{531} = x_{531 \\mod 10} = x_1 = 211, \\]\n\\[ x_{753} = x_{753 \\mod 10} = x_3 = 420, \\]\n\\[ x_{975} = x_{975 \\mod 10} = x_5 = 267. \\]\n\nSo, the value of \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\) is:\n\n\\[ 211 + 420 + 267 = 898. \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Initial values\nx = [211, 375, 420, 523]\n\n# Calculate the next terms to confirm the periodicity\nfor n in range(4, 15):\n    x_n = x[n-1] - x[n-2] + x[n-3] - x[n-4]\n    x.append(x_n)\n\n# Check the periodicity\nprint(x)\n```\n```output\n[211, 375, 420, 523, 267, -211, -375, -420, -523, -267, 211, 375, 420, 523, 267]\n```\nThe computed sequence confirms the periodicity with a period of 10. The values are:\n\n\\[ x_1 = 211, \\]\n\\[ x_2 = 375, \\]\n\\[ x_3 = 420, \\]\n\\[ x_4 = 523, \\]\n\\[ x_5 = 267, \\]\n\\[ x_6 = -211, \\]\n\\[ x_7 = -375, \\]\n\\[ x_8 = -420, \\]\n\\[ x_9 = -523, \\]\n\\[ x_{10} = -267, \\]\n\\[ x_{11} = 211, \\]\n\\[ x_{12} = 375, \\]\n\\[ x_{13} = 420, \\]\n\\[ x_{14} = 523, \\]\n\\[ x_{15} = 267. \\]\n\nSince the sequence is periodic with a period of 10, we can find the values of \\(x_{531}\\), \\(x_{753}\\), and \\(x_{975}\\) as follows:\n\n\\[ x_{531} = x_{531 \\mod 10} = x_1 = 211, \\]\n\\[ x_{753} = x_{753 \\mod 10} = x_3 = 420, \\]\n\\[ x_{975} = x_{975 \\mod 10} = x_