odicity\nperiod = 10\nx_11 = x[11 % period]\nx_12 = x[12 % period]\nx_531 = x[531 % period]\nx_753 = x[753 % period]\nx_975 = x[975 % period]\n\n# Calculate the sum\nresult = x_531 + x_753 + x_975\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n898\n```\nThe value of \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\) is \\(\\boxed{898}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to first generate the sequence according to the given recurrence relation and then find the values of \\(x_{531}\\), \\(x_{753}\\), and \\(x_{975}\\). Finally, we will sum these values.\n\nThe recurrence relation is:\n\\[ x_n = x_{n-1} - x_{n-2} + x_{n-3} - x_{n-4} \\]\nfor \\( n \\geq 5 \\), with initial conditions:\n\\[ x_1 = 211, \\quad x_2 = 375, \\quad x_3 = 420, \\quad x_4 = 523. \\]\n\nWe can generate the sequence using a loop in Python. Let's write the code to generate the sequence and find the required values.\n```python\n# Initial values\nx = [211, 375, 420, 523]\n\n# Generate the sequence up to at least the 975th term\nfor n in range(4, 1000):\n    x_n = x[n-1] - x[n-2] + x[n-3] - x[n-4]\n    x.append(x_n)\n\n# Extract the required terms\nx_531 = x[530]\nx_753 = x[752]\nx_975 = x[974]\n\n# Calculate the sum\nresult = x_531 + x_753 + x_975\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n898\n```\nThe value of \\(x_{531} + x_{753} + x_{975}\\) is \\(\\boxed{898}\\).", "To solve the problem, we need to find the values of \\( p \\) that satisfy both inequalities \\( 0 \\ge 54p - 144 \\) and \\( 0 > 12 - 20p \\). Let's break down the problem step-by-step:\n\n1. Solve the first inequality \\( 0 \\ge 54p - 144 \\):\n\\[ 0 \\ge 54p - 144 \\]\n\\[ 144 \\ge 54p \\]\n\\[ \\frac{144}{54} \\ge p \\]\n\\[ \\frac{8}{3} \\ge p \\]\n\\[ p \\le \\frac{8}{3} \\]\n\n2. Solve the second inequality \\( 0 > 12 - 20p \\):\n\\[ 0 > 12 - 20p \\]\n\\[ 20p > 12 \\]\n\\[ p > \\frac{12}{20} \\]\n\\[ p > \\frac{3}{5} \\]\n\n3. Combine the solutions of both inequalities:\n\\[ \\frac{3}{5} < p \\le \\frac{8}{3} \\]\n\nThe solution in interval notation is \\( \\left( \