rs of each number when divided by 9:\n\n- \\(1 \\mod 9 = 1\\)\n- \\(12 \\mod 9 = 3\\) (since \\(12 = 9 \\cdot 1 + 3\\))\n- \\(123 \\mod 9 = 6\\) (since \\(123 = 9 \\cdot 13 + 6\\))\n- \\(1234 \\mod 9 = 1\\) (since \\(1234 = 9 \\cdot 137 + 1\\))\n- \\(12345 \\mod 9 = 6\\) (since \\(12345 = 9 \\cdot 1371 + 6\\))\n- \\(123456 \\mod 9 = 3\\) (since \\(123456 = 9 \\cdot 13717 + 3\\))\n- \\(1234567 \\mod 9 = 1\\) (since \\(1234567 = 9 \\cdot 137174 + 1\\))\n- \\(12345678 \\mod 9 = 0\\) (since \\(12345678 = 9 \\cdot 1371742\\))\n\nNow we sum these remainders: \\(1 + 3 + 6 + 1 + 6 + 3 + 1 + 0 = 21\\). Finally, we find the remainder when 21 is divided by 9:\n\n\\[21 \\mod 9 = 3\\]\n\nSo, the value of \\(n\\) is 3. Let's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the numbers\nnumbers = [1, 12, 123, 1234, 12345, 123456, 1234567, 12345678]\n\n# Calculate the sum of the remainders when each number is divided by 9\nremainder_sum = sum(number % 9 for number in numbers)\n\n# Find the remainder of this sum when divided by 9\nfinal_remainder = remainder_sum % 9\nprint(final_remainder)\n```\n```output\n3\n```\nThe value of \\( n \\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).", "To solve this problem, we need to find the sum of the numbers \\(1 + 12 + 123 + 1234 + 12345 + 123456 + 1234567 + 12345678\\) and then determine the remainder when this sum is divided by 9.\n\nWe can use the property of modular arithmetic that allows us to take the modulo of each term individually and then sum the results. This simplifies our task significantly because calculating the modulo of each number by 9 is straightforward.\n\nLet's calculate the sum modulo 9 step-by-step:\n\n1. Calculate each number modulo 9.\n2. Sum these results.\n3. Take the sum modulo 9 to get the final answer.\n\nHere is the Python code to perform these steps:\n\n```python\n# Define the numbers\nnumbers = [1, 12, 123, 1234, 12345, 123456, 1234567, 12345678]\n\n# Calculate the sum modulo 9\nsum_mod_9 = sum(num % 9 for num in numbers) % 9\n\nprin