s us two equations: x-4 = 12 and x-4 = -12\r\n\r\n# Solve for x in both cases\r\nx1 = 4 + 12\r\nx2 = 4 - 12\r\n\r\n# Calculate the product of the solutions\r\nproduct_of_solutions = x1 * x2\r\nprint(product_of_solutions)\n```\n```output\n-128\n```\nThe product of all possible values of $x$ is $\\boxed{-128}$.", "To solve the equation \\(|x-4| - 10 = 2\\), we first isolate the absolute value expression:\n\n\\[|x-4| = 12\\]\n\nThe equation \\(|x-4| = 12\\) means that \\(x-4 = 12\\) or \\(x-4 = -12\\). Solving these two equations gives us:\n\n\\[x-4 = 12 \\implies x = 16\\]\n\\[x-4 = -12 \\implies x = -8\\]\n\nSo the possible values of \\(x\\) are 16 and -8. The product of these values is:\n\n\\[16 \\times (-8) = -128\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the possible values of x\nx1 = 4 + 12\nx2 = 4 - 12\n\n# Calculate the product of the possible values of x\nproduct = x1 * x2\nprint(product)\n```\n```output\n-128\n```\nThe product of all possible values of \\(x\\) is \\(\\boxed{-128}\\).", "To solve the equation \\(|x-4| - 10 = 2\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Isolate the absolute value expression:\n\\[|x-4| = 12\\]\n\n2. The absolute value equation \\(|x-4| = 12\\) means that \\(x-4 = 12\\) or \\(x-4 = -12\\). We can solve these two equations separately:\n\\[x-4 = 12 \\implies x = 16\\]\n\\[x-4 = -12 \\implies x = -8\\]\n\n3. The possible values of \\(x\\) are 16 and -8. The product of these values is:\n\\[16 \\times (-8) = -128\\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the possible values of x\nx1 = 16\nx2 = -8\n\n# Calculate the product of the possible values of x\nproduct = x1 * x2\nprint(product)\n```\n```output\n-128\n```\nThe product of all possible values of \\(x\\) is \\(\\boxed{-128}\\).", "To solve the equation \\( |x-4| - 10 = 2 \\), we first isolate the absolute value expression:\n\n\\[ |x-4| = 12 \\]\n\nThe equation \\( |x-4| = 12 \\) means that \\( x-4 \\) is either 12 or -12. S