f the smaller circle within the larger circle is \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 1^2 (\\theta - \\sin \\theta) = \\frac{\\theta - \\sin \\theta}{2}\\), where \\(\\theta\\) is the central angle in radians.\n   - The area of the segment is also \\(\\pi - \\left(4\\pi - \\frac{5\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\pi - \\frac{7\\pi}{3} = -\\frac{4\\pi}{3}\\), which is not possible. This indicates that the segment of the smaller circle within the larger circle is actually part of the shaded region.\n\nLet's use Python and SymPy to solve for the angle \\(\\theta\\):\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the angle theta in radians\ntheta = sp.symbols('theta')\n\n# The area of the segment of the smaller circle within the larger circle\nsegment_area = (theta - sp.sin(theta)) / 2\n\n# The area of the shaded region is 5/12 of the area of the larger circle\nshaded_area = 5 * sp.pi / 3\n\n# The area of the smaller circle is pi\nsmall_circle_area = sp.pi\n\n# The area of the segment of the smaller circle within the larger circle is part of the shaded region\n# So, the area of the segment is small_circle_area - (large_circle_area - shaded_area)\nsegment_area_eq = sp.Eq(segment_area, small_circle_area - (4 * sp.pi - shaded_area))\n\n# Solve for theta\ntheta_solution = sp.solve(segment_area_eq, theta)\ntheta_degrees = [sp.deg(sol.evalf()) for sol in theta_solution if sol.evalf() > 0 and sol.evalf() < sp.pi]\n\nprint(theta_degrees)\n```\n```output\nNo algorithms are implemented to solve equation theta/2 - sin(theta)/2 - 13*pi/6\n```\nIt seems that the equation we set up is not straightforward to solve algebraically. Instead, we can use numerical methods to find the value of \\(\\theta\\). Let's use SymPy's `nsolve` function to find the numerical solution.\n\nHere's the updated code:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the angle theta in radians\ntheta = sp.symbols('theta')\n\n# The area of the segment of the smaller circle within the larger circle\nsegment_area = (theta - sp.sin(theta)) / 2\