 between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$ by $\\theta$. We can use the following steps:\n\n1. Use the given angle between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ to express the dot product $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}$ in terms of the magnitudes of $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$.\n2. Use the given angle between $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$ to express the dot product $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b})$ in terms of the magnitudes of $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$.\n3. Use the dot product properties to find the angle $\\theta$ between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$.\n\nLet's start by expressing the given information in mathematical terms:\n\n1. The angle between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is $29^\\circ$, so:\n   \\[\n   \\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ)\n   \\]\n\n2. The angle between $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$ is $84^\\circ$, so:\n   \\[\n   \\mathbf{b} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) = \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(84^\\circ)\n   \\]\n   Expanding the dot product, we get:\n   \\[\n   \\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{b} = \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(84^\\circ)\n   \\]\n   Using $\\mathbf{b} \\cdot \\mathbf{a} = \\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}$, we get:\n   \\[\n   \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ) - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\|^2 = \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(84^\\circ)\n   \\]\n   Dividing both sides by $\\|\\mathbf{b}\\|$ (assuming $\\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\neq 0$), we get:\n   \\[\n   \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\cos(29^\\circ) - \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| = \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}\\| \\cos(84^\\circ)\n   \\]\n\n3. Now we need to find the angle $\\theta$ between $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}$. Using the dot product, we have:\n   \\[\n   \\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{a} - \\mathbf{b}) = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{a} - \\