ls('x')\n\n# Define the tangent of theta\ntan_theta = x / 11\n\n# Define the tangent of 3*theta\ntan_3theta = (3 * tan_theta - tan_theta**3) / (1 - 3 * tan_theta**2)\n\n# Since tan(3*theta) = BD / DM, and DM = 1 (since AD = 10 and AM = 11)\n# We have BD = sqrt(21 + x^2) and DM = 1\n# So, tan(3*theta) = sqrt(21 + x^2) / 1 = sqrt(21 + x^2)\ntan_3theta_expr = sp.sqrt(21 + x**2)\n\n# Set up the equation\nequation = sp.Eq(tan_3theta, tan_3theta_expr)\n\n# Solve for x\nx_solution = sp.solve(equation, x)\nx_value = x_solution[0]\n\n# Calculate the length of AB\nAB = sp.sqrt(121 + x_value**2)\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of triangle ABC\nperimeter = 2 * AB + 2 * x_value\n\n# Simplify the perimeter\nperimeter_simplified = sp.simplify(perimeter)\nprint(perimeter_simplified)\n```\n```output\n-22 + 2*sqrt(253)\n```\nIt looks like we have obtained a negative value for \\(x\\), which is not physically meaningful in this context. We should consider the positive solution for \\(x\\). Let's re-evaluate the solution and ensure we are selecting the correct, positive value for \\(x\\).\n\nWe can modify the code to explicitly select the positive solution for \\(x\\):\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\nx = sp.symbols('x')\n\n# Define the tangent of theta\ntan_theta = x / 11\n\n# Define the tangent of 3*theta\ntan_3theta = (3 * tan_theta - tan_theta**3) / (1 - 3 * tan_theta**2)\n\n# Since tan(3*theta) = BD / DM, and DM = 1 (since AD = 10 and AM = 11)\n# We have BD = sqrt(21 + x^2) and DM = 1\n# So, tan(3*theta) = sqrt(21 + x^2) / 1 = sqrt(21 + x^2)\ntan_3theta_expr = sp.sqrt(21 + x**2)\n\n# Set up the equation\nequation = sp.Eq(tan_3theta, tan_3theta_expr)\n\n# Solve for x\nx_solution = sp.solve(equation, x)\nx_value = [sol.evalf() for sol in x_solution if sol.is_real and sol > 0][0]\n\n# Calculate the length of AB\nAB = sp.sqrt(121 + x_value**2)\n\n# Calculate the perimeter of triangle ABC\nperimeter = 2 * AB + 2 * x_value\n\n# Simplify the perimeter\nperimeter_si