11}\n     \\]\n   - Using the tangent function for \\(\\angle BDC\\):\n     \\[\n     \\tan(3\\theta) = \\frac{2x}{1}\n     \\]\n   - We know the triple angle formula for tangent:\n     \\[\n     \\tan(3\\theta) = \\frac{3\\tan(\\theta) - \\tan^3(\\theta)}{1 - 3\\tan^2(\\theta)}\n     \\]\n     Substituting \\(\\tan(\\theta) = \\frac{x}{11}\\):\n     \\[\n     \\frac{2x}{1} = \\frac{3\\left(\\frac{x}{11}\\right) - \\left(\\frac{x}{11}\\right)^3}{1 - 3\\left(\\frac{x}{11}\\right)^2}\n     \\]\n     Simplifying:\n     \\[\n     2x = \\frac{\\frac{3x}{11} - \\frac{x^3}{1331}}{1 - \\frac{3x^2}{121}}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     2x = \\frac{\\frac{3x \\cdot 121 - x^3}{1331}}{\\frac{121 - 3x^2}{121}}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     2x = \\frac{363x - x^3}{1331} \\cdot \\frac{121}{121 - 3x^2}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     2x = \\frac{363x - x^3}{11(121 - 3x^2)}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     2x \\cdot 11(121 - 3x^2) = 363x - x^3\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     22x(121 - 3x^2) = 363x - x^3\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     2662x - 66x^3 = 363x - x^3\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     2662x - 363x = 66x^3 - x^3\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     2299x = 65x^3\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     2299 = 65x^2\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     x^2 = \\frac{2299}{65}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     x = \\sqrt{\\frac{2299}{65}}\n     \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the Perimeter:**\n   - The length of \\(AB\\) and \\(AC\\) is:\n     \\[\n     AB = AC = \\sqrt{11^2 + x^2} = \\sqrt{121 + \\frac{2299}{65}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{121 \\cdot 65 + 2299}{65}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{7864 + 2299}{65}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{10163}{65}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{10163}{65}}\n     \\]\n   - The perimeter of triangle \\(ABC\\) is:\n     \\[\n     2AB + BC = 2\\sqrt{\\frac{10163}{65}} + 2x = 2\\sqrt{\\frac{10163}{65}} + 2\\sqrt{\\frac{2299}{65}} = 2\\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{10163}{65}} + \\sqrt{\\frac{2299}{65}}\\right)\n     \\]\n\nLet's calculate the exact value using Python.\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given values\nAM = 11\nAD = 10\nDM = AM - AD\n\n# Calculate x^2\nx_squared = 2299 / 65\n\n# Calculate x\n