mum value of \\(|a| + |b| + |c|\\).\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define variables\na, b, c = sp.symbols(\'a b c\')\n\n# Define the constraints\nconstraints = [\n    sp.Abs(c) <= 1,\n    sp.Abs(a/4 + b/2 + c) <= 1,\n    sp.Abs(a + b + c) <= 1\n]\n\n# Define the expression to maximize\nexpression = sp.Abs(a) + sp.Abs(b) + sp.Abs(c)\n\n# We will test some possible values of a, b, and c that satisfy the constraints\n# and find the maximum value of the expression\n\n# Let\'s test the values a = 4, b = -4, c = 1\na_val = 4\nb_val = -4\nc_val = 1\n\n# Check if these values satisfy the constraints\nconstraint1 = sp.Abs(c_val) <= 1\nconstraint2 = sp.Abs(a_val/4 + b_val/2 + c_val) <= 1\nconstraint3 = sp.Abs(a_val + b_val + c_val) <= 1\n\n# Calculate the expression value\nexpression_value = sp.Abs(a_val) + sp.Abs(b_val) + sp.Abs(c_val)\n\n# Print the results\nprint(f"Constraint 1: {constraint1}")\nprint(f"Constraint 2: {constraint2}")\nprint(f"Constraint 3: {constraint3}")\nprint(f"Expression value: {expression_value}")\n```\n```output\nConstraint 1: True\nConstraint 2: True\nConstraint 3: True\nExpression value: 9\n```\nThe output shows that the values \\(a = 4\\), \\(b = -4\\), and \\(c = 1\\) satisfy all the constraints, and the value of \\(|a| + |b| + |c|\\) is 9. This means that the maximum possible value of \\(|a| + |b| + |c|\\) is 9.\n\nThus, the largest possible value of \\(|a| + |b| + |c|\\) is \\(\\boxed{9}\\).', "To solve this problem, we need to find the maximum possible value of \\( |a| + |b| + |c| \\) given the constraint \\( |ax^2 + bx + c| \\le 1 \\) for all \\( 0 \\le x \\le 1 \\). This means that the quadratic function \\( f(x) = ax^2 + bx + c \\) must lie between -1 and 1 for all \\( x \\) in the interval \\([0, 1]\\).\n\nWe can use the values of \\( f(x) \\) at the endpoints and the midpoint of the interval to help us determine the coefficients \\( a \\), \\( b \\), and \\( c \\). Specifically, we will evaluate \\( f(x) \\) at \\( x = 0 \\), \\( x 