ituting \\( x = 0 \\) into the polynomial.\n\nLet's calculate this step-by-step using Python.\n```python\n# Define the polynomial function f(x)\ndef f(x):\n    return 3*x**4 + 5*x**2 - 9*x - 2\n\n# Calculate f(0) which is the sum of the coefficients of g(x) = f(x-1)\nsum_of_coefficients = f(0)\nprint(sum_of_coefficients)\n```\n```output\n-2\n```\nThe sum of the coefficients of the polynomial \\( g(x) = f(x-1) \\) is the same as the value of \\( f(0) \\), which is \\(-2\\).\n\nTherefore, the sum of the coefficients of \\( g(x) \\) is \\(\\boxed{-2}\\).", "To find the sum of the coefficients of the polynomial \\(g(x) = f(x-1)\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Define the polynomial \\(f(x) = 3x^4 + 5x^2 - 9x - 2\\).\n2. Substitute \\(x-1\\) into \\(f(x)\\) to get \\(g(x) = f(x-1)\\).\n3. Expand the polynomial \\(g(x)\\).\n4. Find the sum of the coefficients of \\(g(x)\\).\n\nThe sum of the coefficients of a polynomial \\(P(x)\\) is simply \\(P(1)\\). So, we can find \\(g(1) = f(1-1) = f(0)\\).\n\nLet's implement this in Python using sympy:\n\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the variable\nx = sp.symbols('x')\n\n# Define the polynomial f(x)\nf = 3*x**4 + 5*x**2 - 9*x - 2\n\n# Substitute x-1 into f(x) to get g(x)\ng = f.subs(x, x-1)\n\n# Simplify g(x)\ng = sp.expand(g)\n\n# The sum of the coefficients of g(x) is g(1)\nsum_of_coefficients = g.subs(x, 1)\n\nprint(sum_of_coefficients)\n```\n```output\n-9\n```\nThe sum of the coefficients of the polynomial \\(g(x) = f(x-1)\\) is \\(\\boxed{-9}\\).", "To find the sum of the coefficients of the polynomial \\( g(x) \\), we need to evaluate \\( g(1) \\). Since \\( g(x) = f(x-1) \\), we have \\( g(1) = f(1-1) = f(0) \\).\n\nGiven the polynomial \\( f(x) = 3x^4 + 5x^2 - 9x - 2 \\), we can find \\( f(0) \\) by substituting \\( x = 0 \\) into the polynomial.\n\nLet's calculate \\( f(0) \\):\n\n\\[ f(0) = 3(0)^4 + 5(0)^2 - 9(0) - 2 = -2 \\]\n\nSo, the sum of the coefficients of \\( g(x) \\) is \\( -2 \\).\n\nLet's confirm