al point.\n\nLet's start by converting $\\frac{137}{500}$ into its decimal form. We can do this by performing the division $137 \\div 500$.\n\nThe decimal expansion of $\\frac{137}{500}$ is $0.274$. The last nonzero digit to the right of the decimal point is $4$.\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the decimal expansion of 137/500\ndecimal_expansion = 137 / 500\n\n# Convert to string to find the last nonzero digit\ndecimal_str = str(decimal_expansion)\n\n# Find the last nonzero digit to the right of the decimal point\nnonzero_digits = [digit for digit in decimal_str if digit != '0' and digit != '.']\nlast_nonzero_digit = nonzero_digits[-1]\n\nprint(last_nonzero_digit)\n```\n```output\n4\n```\nThe last nonzero digit to the right of the decimal point in the decimal expansion of $\\frac{137}{500}$ is \\(\\boxed{4}\\).", 'To determine the last nonzero digit to the right of the decimal point in the decimal expansion of $\\frac{137}{500}$, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Compute the decimal expansion of $\\frac{137}{500}$.\n2. Identify the last nonzero digit to the right of the decimal point.\n\nFirst, let\'s convert $\\frac{137}{500}$ to its decimal form. We can do this by dividing 137 by 500.\n\n\\[\n\\frac{137}{500} = 0.274\n\\]\n\nThe decimal expansion of $\\frac{137}{500}$ is $0.274$. The last nonzero digit to the right of the decimal point is 4.\n\nLet\'s confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the decimal expansion of 137/500\ndecimal_expansion = 137 / 500\n\n# Convert the decimal expansion to a string to identify the last nonzero digit\ndecimal_str = str(decimal_expansion)\n\n# Find the last nonzero digit to the right of the decimal point\n# We need to strip off the "0." at the start and then find the last nonzero digit\ndecimal_part = decimal_str.split(\'.\')[1]\nlast_nonzero_digit = next(digit for digit in reversed(decimal_part) if digit != \'0\')\n\nprint(last_nonzero_digit)\n```\n```output\n4\n```\nThe last nonzero d