ives the remainder of a division of one number by another.\n\nThe mathematical expression for this is \\(54 \\mod 6\\). The result of this operation will be the remainder when 54 is divided by 6.\n\nLet's calculate this using Python code.\n```python\n# Calculate the remainder when 54 is divided by 6\nremainder = 54 % 6\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nThe remainder when 54 is divided by 6 is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).", "To find the remainder when 54 is divided by 6, we can use the modulus operation. The modulus operation (%) returns the remainder of the division of the left operand by the right operand.\n\nHere's the step-by-step reasoning and the Python code to compute the result:\n\n1. Perform the division of 54 by 6.\n2. The quotient is 9 and the remainder is 0.\n\nLet's use Python to confirm this.\n```python\n# Calculate the remainder of 54 divided by 6\nremainder = 54 % 6\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nThe remainder when 54 is divided by 6 is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).", 'The remainder of 54 divided by 6 is 0, because 54 is exactly divisible by 6. \\boxed{0}\n\n\\boxed{0}', "To solve the problem of finding the remainder when 54 is divided by 6, we can use the modulo operation. The modulo operation, denoted by the % symbol in many programming languages, gives the remainder of a division of two numbers. In this case, we need to compute \\(54 \\mod 6\\).\n\nLet's write the Python code to find the remainder:\n\n```python\n# Calculate the remainder of 54 divided by 6\nremainder = 54 % 6\nprint(remainder)\n```\n```output\n0\n```\nThe remainder when 54 is divided by 6 is \\(\\boxed{0}\\).", "To determine the remainder of \\(54 \\mod 6\\), we need to find the integer \\(r\\) such that \\(0 \\leq r < 6\\) and \\(54 = 6q + r\\) for some integer \\(q\\). The value of \\(r\\) is the remainder when 54 is divided by 6.\n\nLet's perform the division step by step:\n\n1. Divide 54 by 6:\n   \\[\n   54 \\div 6 = 9\n   \\]\n   This tells us that 6 goes into 54 exactly 9 time