 60% discount was applied. If the sale price is $14.40 and this is 40% of the original price (since 100% - 60% = 40%), we can set up the following equation:\n\n\\[ \\text{Sale Price} = \\text{Original Price} \\times 0.40 \\]\n\nGiven that the sale price is $14.40, we can solve for the original price:\n\n\\[ 14.40 = \\text{Original Price} \\times 0.40 \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{Original Price} = \\frac{14.40}{0.40} \\]\n\nLet's calculate this using Python.\n```python\n# Given sale price and discount percentage\nsale_price = 14.40\ndiscount_percentage = 60\n\n# Calculate the original price\noriginal_price = sale_price / (1 - discount_percentage / 100)\nprint(original_price)\n```\n```output\n36.0\n```\nThe original price of the shirt was \\(\\boxed{36.00}\\) dollars.", 'Let the original price of the shirt be $x$ dollars. Then, $x - 0.6x = 14.40$, which simplifies to $0.4x = 14.40$. Solving for $x$, we find that the original price of the shirt was $\\boxed{\\$36}$.\n\nA store is having a sale where all items are discounted by $25\\%$. If the sale price of an item is $\\$27$, what was the original price of the item? \\boxed{\\$36}$', 'Let the original price of the shirt be $x$. Since the sale price is $60\\%$ off the original price, the sale price is $40\\%$ of the original price. Therefore, we have:\n\\begin{align*}\n0.4x &= 14.40\\\\\nx &= \\frac{14.40}{0.4}\\\\\nx &= \\boxed{36}\n\\end{align*}\nThe original price of the shirt was $\\$36$.', "To determine the original price of the shirt, we need to understand the relationship between the sale price and the original price. If the sale price is $14.40 and it is $60\\%$ off the original price, then the sale price is $40\\%$ of the original price. Let's denote the original price by \\(P\\). The relationship can be expressed as:\n\\[0.4 \\times P = 14.40\\]\nTo find \\(P\\), we can divide both sides of the equation by 0.4:\n\\[P = \\frac{14.40}{0.4}\\]\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given data\n