ice = sale_price / (1 - discount_percentage)\nprint(original_price)\n```\n```output\n36.0\n```\nThe original price of the shirt was \\(\\boxed{36}\\) dollars.", "To find the original price of the shirt, we need to understand the relationship between the sale price and the original price. If the sale price is $14.40 and it is $60\\%$ off the original price, then the sale price represents $40\\%$ of the original price. Let's denote the original price by $x$. The relationship can be expressed as:\n\\[ 0.4x = 14.40 \\]\nTo find $x$, we can solve the equation by dividing both sides by $0.4$:\n\\[ x = \\frac{14.40}{0.4} \\]\nLet's calculate this using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Given data\nsale_price = 14.40\npercentage_off = 0.60\n\n# Calculate the original price\noriginal_price = sale_price / (1 - percentage_off)\nprint(original_price)\n```\n```output\n36.0\n```\nThe original price of the shirt was \\(\\boxed{36}\\) dollars.", 'We know that $\\$14.40$ is $40\\%$ of the original price, so the original price is $\\frac{100}{40}\\cdot\\$14.40=\\boxed{\\$36.00}$', "To find the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we need to analyze the behavior of the function within this interval.\n\nThe function \\( f(x) \\) is composed of three absolute value functions. The critical points where the behavior of the function changes are at \\( x = p \\), \\( x = 15 \\), and \\( x = p + 15 \\). However, since we are only considering the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we only need to consider the points \\( x = p \\) and \\( x = 15 \\).\n\nLet's evaluate the function at these points:\n\n1. When \\( x = p \\):\n\\[ f(p) = |p - p| + |p - 15| + |p - p - 15| = 0 + |p - 15| + |-15| = 15 + (15 - p) = 30 - p \\]\n\n2. When \\( x = 15 \\):\n\\[ f(15) = |15 - p| + |15 - 15| + |15 - p - 15| = |15 - p| + 0 + |-p| = 15 - p + p = 15 \\]\n\nSince \\( 0 < p < 15 \\), it follows that \\( 30 - p > 15 \\). Therefore, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\( 15 \\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code.\n```python\n# Define the function f(x)\ndef f(x, p):\n    return abs(x - p) + abs(x - 15) + abs(x - p - 15)\n\n# Define the interval p <= x <= 15\np = 7  # Example value for p (0 < p < 15)\nx_values = [p, 15]  # Critical points in the interval\n\n# Evaluate the function at the critical points\nf_values = [f(x, p) for x in x_values]\n\n# Find the minimum value\nmin_value = min(f_values)\nprint(min_value)\n```\n```output\n15\n```\nThe minimum value taken by the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( x \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).", "To determine the minimum value of the function \\( f(x) = |x - p| + |x - 15| + |x - p - 15| \\) for \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), we need to analyze the behavior of the function within this interval.\n\nThe function \\( f(x) \\) is composed of three absolute value terms. The critical points where the behavior of the absolute value terms change are \\( x = p \\), \\( x = 15 \\), and \\( x = p + 15 \\). However, since we are only considering the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\), the critical points we need to consider are \\( x = p \\) and \\( x = 15 \\).\n\nLet's evaluate the function at these critical points:\n\n1. When \\( x = p \\):\n\\[ f(p) = |p - p| + |p - 15| + |p - p - 15| = 0 + |p - 15| + |-15| = 15 + (15 - p) = 30 - p. \\]\n\n2. When \\( x = 15 \\):\n\\[ f(15) = |15 - p| + |15 - 15| + |15 - p - 15| = |15 - p| + 0 + | - p| = (15 - p) + p = 15. \\]\n\nSince \\( 0 < p < 15 \\), it is clear that \\( 30 - p > 15 \\). Therefore, the minimum value of \\( f(x) \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is 15, which occurs at \\( x = 15 \\).\n\nThus, the minimum value taken by \\( f(x) \\) for \\( x \\) in the interval \\( p \\leq x \\leq 15 \\) is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n